I with my little eye, something red. Is that red card?

00:29:03.320 --> 00:29:05.080
- Today we're at the flea market.

00:29:05.080 --> 00:29:06.680
It is the perfect place to play

00:29:06.680 --> 00:29:09.700
one of our very favorite games, I Spy.

00:29:09.700 --> 00:29:12.360
First you choose one of the players to be the spy.

00:29:12.360 --> 00:29:15.240
Then the spy silently chooses an object

00:29:15.240 --> 00:29:17.800
and then reveals the object to the other players

00:29:17.800 --> 00:29:22.060
by saying I spy with my little eye something blue.

00:29:22.060 --> 00:29:23.540
Then the other players try to guess

00:29:23.540 --> 00:29:25.480
what the secret object is.

00:29:25.480 --> 00:29:29.030
I spy with my little eye something red.

00:29:29.030 --> 00:29:30.000
- Is it that notebook?

00:29:30.480 --> 00:29:31.740
- No, good guess.

00:29:31.740 --> 00:29:34.740
If the players are having trouble finding the secret object,

00:29:34.740 --> 00:29:36.800
then the spy can give an additional hint.

00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:37.760
- I'll give you a hint.

00:29:37.760 --> 00:29:39.250
Look up.

00:29:39.250 --> 00:29:42.620
- Is it that red, white, and blue?

00:29:42.620 --> 00:29:45.200
- Mailbox, yes, that's exactly what it is.

00:29:45.200 --> 00:29:46.240
You got it.

00:29:46.240 --> 00:29:47.940
All that matters is that you're making kids

00:29:47.940 --> 00:29:49.400
think about their surroundings

00:29:49.400 --> 00:29:51.710
and exposing them to new words.

00:29:51.710 --> 00:29:52.550
- Bye.
